## Contract (raw three.js ESM module)
{{ frame_doc }}
{{ contract }}
- `{{ asset_file }}` must `export function build{{ asset_name }}(THREE, opts = {}) { ... return group; }`
  where `group` is a `THREE.Group` whose lowest point is at y=0 and whose footprint is centred on
  the origin, sized as stated (±5%). `opts.seed` (number) and `opts.variant` (0..n) may vary
  details deterministically (use a tiny mulberry32 PRNG inside the file — never Math.random).
- Build from primitives (Box/Cylinder/Cone/Sphere/Lathe/Extrude/Tube) with MeshStandardMaterial
  colours in hex; merge repeated pieces with InstancedMesh when > 20 copies.
- Set `group.userData.size = [w, h, d]` to the measured size.  Optional animation hook:
  `group.userData.update = (t, dt) => {...}` (the zone that places you caches it and calls it;
  `userData.tick` is never called by anything).  Amplitudes must be visible after 1.5 s:
  >= 0.10 rad of rotation or >= 0.05 m of travel — not sub-centimetre jitter.
- No DOM, no texture/image loading, no fetch, no imports except `import * as THREE from 'three'`.
- ≤ 15k triangles per instance; segments 12-24.
{% endif %}

## DO / DON'T
- DO use the exact size numbers above; the zone builders rely on them.
- DO give it the 3-4 recognisable features a person would name (a stone lantern: base, post, light
  box with 4 windows, curved roof, finial) — plus 2-3 pieces of wear or incident that make it look
  used: a chipped corner, a leaning post, moss at the base, a rope, a hanging tool.
- DO make `opts.variant` (0..n) change the SILHOUETTE, not just the scale: at least 3 visibly
  different versions (a different crown shape, a different roof pitch, a broken vs whole rail).
  Zones rely on this for variety, so a plain `variant` that only scales is a wasted asset.
- DO give any repeated natural asset per-instance hue room: expose `opts.hue`/`opts.tint` (or
  accept `opts.seed` and vary the colour from it) so 20 copies are not one colour.
- DON'T model a flat plane with a colour where the thing has real thickness (a fence is stalks and
  rails, not a textured quad) — closeups are judged.
- DON'T leave floating pieces: every sub-shape overlaps a neighbour by ≥ 2 mm.
- DON'T write anything but the asset file.
